# What Docker never needs to receive.
#
# Without this file the whole working tree is sent to the daemon as build
# context, .git included, while the Dockerfile copies four directories. The
# context is transferred before the first instruction runs, so it is paid on
# every build, including the ones that hit the layer cache and produce nothing.
#
# The UN card set left the repository and the image entirely: the "Generate
# UN cards" workflow publishes it as a GitHub Release, and an administrator
# imports it into the persistent data volume. Nothing card-shaped may creep
# back into the build context — a generated set on a developer machine is
# excluded below.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Node dependencies are installed inside the frontend build stage.
node_modules
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/.review-bridge

# Local settings and credentials never belong in the build context.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Python bytecode and virtualenvs.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv

# Local runtime data: the database, exports and the generated secret key. Never
# part of an image, and shipping them would mean shipping someone's data.
data
exports

# Test and tooling output.
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
coverage
htmlcov
*.log

# Documentation and repository furniture. The application does not read these —
# except the changelog, which the what's-new card serves after an update.
docs
*.md
!backend/**/*.md
!CHANGELOG.md
scripts
unraid
assets

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Locally generated UN card sets must never enter the image.
un-cards*/
emcargo-un-cards.zip
